{"name":"Stargazing","hex":"#414549","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stargazing","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of stargaze"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of gazing at the stars; astronomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stargazing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stargazing (Myles Smith song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Stargazing\" is a song by British singer-songwriter Myles Smith. It was released as the lead single from his second extended play A Minute... on 10 May 2024 through Sony Music. Smith wrote it with songwriter Jesse Fink and its producer, Peter Fenn. It was later included on Smith's first album My Mess, My Heart, My Life."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f2/Myles_Smith_-_Stargazing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stargazing_(Myles_Smith_song)"},{"title":"Stargazing (Travis Scott song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Stargazing\" is a song by American rapper and singer Travis Scott. It was released on August 3, 2018, as the only promotional single and first track off of his third studio album, Astroworld. The song debuted at number eight on the Billboard Hot 100, and was later certified platinum by the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stargazing_(Travis_Scott_song)"},{"title":"Amateur astronomy","blocks":[{"text":"Amateur astronomy is a hobby where participants enjoy observing, studying, or imaging celestial objects in the sky using the unaided eye, binoculars, telescopes, and other gadgets. Although scientific research may not be their primary goal, some amateur astronomers contribute to citizen science by monitoring variable stars, double stars, sunspots, and occultations of stars by the Moon or asteroids, as well as by discovering transient astronomical events, such as comets, galactic novae or supernovae in other galaxies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Astronomy_Amateur_3_V2.jpg/330px-Astronomy_Amateur_3_V2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amateur_astronomy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Hans_Oberndorfer_2.JPG/500px-Hans_Oberndorfer_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Hans_Oberndorfer_2.JPG/1280px-Hans_Oberndorfer_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Hans_Oberndorfer_2.JPG/500px-Hans_Oberndorfer_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Amateur astronomer recording observations of the sun.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHans_Oberndorfer_2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Beneath_the_Milky_Way.jpg/500px-Beneath_the_Milky_Way.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Beneath_the_Milky_Way.jpg/1280px-Beneath_the_Milky_Way.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Beneath_the_Milky_Way.jpg/500px-Beneath_the_Milky_Way.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Places like Paranal Observatory offer crystal clear skies for observing astronomical objects with or without instruments.[20]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeneath_the_Milky_Way.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_Cat%27s_Paw_Remastered.jpeg/500px-The_Cat%27s_Paw_Remastered.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_Cat%27s_Paw_Remastered.jpeg/1280px-The_Cat%27s_Paw_Remastered.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_Cat%27s_Paw_Remastered.jpeg/500px-The_Cat%27s_Paw_Remastered.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An image of the Cat's Paw Nebula created combining the work of professional and amateur astronomers. The image is the combination of the 2.2-metre MPG/ESO telescope of the La Silla Observatory in Chile and a 0.4-meter amateur telescope.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Cat's_Paw_Remastered.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Light_pollution_It%27s_not_pretty.jpg/500px-Light_pollution_It%27s_not_pretty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Light_pollution_It%27s_not_pretty.jpg/1280px-Light_pollution_It%27s_not_pretty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Light_pollution_It%27s_not_pretty.jpg/500px-Light_pollution_It%27s_not_pretty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This image contains two side-by-side pictures of the night sky comparing the effects of light pollution on the visibility of celestial objects.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALight_pollution_It's_not_pretty.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Outreach%2C_one_of_the_most_rewarding_jobs_%284798622790%29.jpg/500px-Outreach%2C_one_of_the_most_rewarding_jobs_%284798622790%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Outreach%2C_one_of_the_most_rewarding_jobs_%284798622790%29.jpg/1280p